Category,Question,Answer
Booking & Reservations,How far in advance should I book?,It's recommended to book as early as possible. Many companies accept bookings up to a year in advance with a deposit. Popular dates fill up quickly.
Booking & Reservations,Is a deposit required to reserve a bouncy castle?,Yes. Most companies require a non-refundable deposit (typically €50 or 10-50% of total rental fee) to secure your date. The deposit is applied toward your final balance.
Booking & Reservations,What payment methods are accepted?,Most rental companies accept credit cards. bank transfers. cash. and PayPal. Some may charge a fee for returned payments.
Booking & Reservations,Do you offer discounts for multiple-day rentals?,Yes. many companies offer discounted rates for multi-day rentals or weekday/off-season bookings. Ask about package deals.
Booking & Reservations,Do you have a referral program?,Some companies offer referral credits (e.g. €25 per referral) that can be applied to future bookings.
Cancellation & Weather Policies,What happens if it rains or there's bad weather?,Most companies allow cancellation with full deposit refund if weather makes setup unsafe (high winds over 30km/h or Beaufort scale 5. storms. lightning). Rescheduling is also typically allowed.
Cancellation & Weather Policies,When can I cancel due to weather?,Weather cancellations usually require 24 hours notice. though some companies allow same-day cancellation if conditions are unsafe.
Setup Requirements,How much space do I need?,You need enough space for the inflatable dimensions plus additional clearance (typically 1-1.5 metres) on all sides. Check with your rental company for specific measurements.
Setup Requirements,What type of surface can the bouncy castle be set up on?,Most companies can set up on grass. concrete. asphalt. or indoors. Stakes are used for grass; sandbags may be required for hard surfaces (sometimes at extra cost).
Setup Requirements,What if my setup location is inaccessible or unsafe?,If the delivery team cannot safely set up due to inaccessible terrain. low power lines. or unsafe conditions. the booking fee will not be refunded.
Setup Requirements,Can the bouncy castle be set up indoors?,Yes. many inflatables can be set up indoors in gymnasiums. halls. or large rooms with sufficient ceiling height (typically 4.5+ metres). This is recommended for overnight rentals.
Delivery Setup & Pickup,Who sets up the bouncy castle?,The rental company typically handles delivery. setup. and takedown. Setup usually takes 15-30 minutes.
Delivery Setup & Pickup,What time will delivery and pickup occur?,Delivery is usually scheduled for the morning of your event. and pickup is in the evening or the following day. Standard rentals are typically for 6-8 hour periods.
Delivery Setup & Pickup,Do I need to be present for setup and pickup?,Yes. an adult must be present to sign the rental agreement and receive safety instructions during setup. and to verify condition during pickup.
Delivery Setup & Pickup,Is setup and takedown time counted as part of the rental duration?,Generally no—rental time refers to the period the inflatable is available for use. not including setup and takedown time.
Delivery Setup & Pickup,Can I keep the bouncy castle overnight?,Yes. overnight rentals are available at an additional charge. Overnight rentals should preferably be set up in a secure. enclosed indoor or covered location.
Safety Rules & Supervision,Is adult supervision required?,Yes. adult supervision (age 18+) is required at all times while the inflatable is in use. The supervisor is responsible for enforcing safety rules.
Safety Rules & Supervision,What are the capacity limits?,Standard bounce houses: 6-8 children at a time. Water slides: 1 rider at a time (or 2 for double-lane slides). Combo units: 6 riders maximum. Always follow specific guidelines provided.
Safety Rules & Supervision,Are there age or height restrictions?,Yes. most inflatables have age and height limits. Separate younger children from older/bigger children to prevent injuries. Adults should not bounce inside with small children present.
Safety Rules & Supervision,Do children need to wear socks?,Yes. socks are typically required to protect children's feet from friction burns and to maintain hygiene. Shoes must always be removed.
Safety Rules & Supervision,Can adults use the bouncy castle?,Most standard bouncy castles are designed for children only. However. some companies offer adult-sized inflatables. Never exceed the weight/capacity limits specified.
Safety Rules & Supervision,What items are prohibited in the bouncy castle?,Face paints. glitter. silly string. party poppers. confetti. shoes. glasses. jewelry. food. drinks. gum. candy. pets. climbing on walls or netting. flips. wrestling. and rough play.
Safety Rules & Supervision,Why is silly string prohibited?,Silly string is highly flammable and can damage the inflatable material. Use of silly string typically incurs a cleaning fee of €100 or more.
Insurance & Liability,Is the rental company insured?,Reputable companies carry Public Liability Insurance (minimum €5 million as required by EU regulations). Ask for proof of insurance if needed for schools. churches. or public events.
Insurance & Liability,Am I responsible for injuries or damage?,The renter assumes responsibility for the safety of all users. Most rental agreements require you to sign a liability waiver acknowledging that bouncing is a potentially dangerous activity.
Insurance & Liability,Should I get my own insurance?,Some companies recommend that hirers obtain their own public liability insurance covering their responsibility arising from use of the inflatable. especially for large events or public venues.
Location,Can I set up a bouncy castle in a park or public space?,Yes. but you must secure any necessary permits from the local municipality or council beforehand. Some parks require proof of insurance and may have specific restrictions.
Location,Do I need permission to set up on public property?,Yes. you typically need permits and may need to provide proof of insurance. Check with your local council or municipality well in advance.
Cleaning & Damage,What if the bouncy castle gets damaged during my rental?,You are responsible for damage caused by misuse. negligence. or failure to follow safety rules. Repair costs or replacement fees may apply. Normal wear and tear is typically covered.
Cleaning & Damage,Do I need to clean the bouncy castle before return?,The unit should be returned in the same condition received. Excessive cleaning required due to prohibited items may result in additional cleaning fees (€25-€100+).
Cleaning & Damage,What if the equipment malfunctions?,Stop use immediately and contact the rental company. Do not attempt to repair the equipment yourself.
Cleaning & Damage,Should I turn off the blower if it rains?,The blower should be kept running continuously during use. If rain occurs. evacuate the inflatable and cover the blower to prevent electrical hazards.
Pricing & Additional Fees,What is included in the rental price?,Most rental prices include the inflatable unit. delivery. setup. and takedown. However. always confirm as some companies charge separately for delivery or cleaning.
Pricing & Additional Fees,How much does it cost to rent a bouncy castle?,Prices vary by size. type. and location: Small basic bounce houses: €100-€250. Larger combo units: €250-€500. Water slides/obstacle courses: €300-€800. Multi-day rentals often receive discounts.
General Questions,How are the bouncy castles cleaned?,Reputable companies clean and disinfect units after each use. Ask about their specific cleaning procedures if hygiene is a concern.
General Questions,Can I move the bouncy castle once it's set up?,No. never attempt to move the inflatable once it has been set up by the delivery team. This can damage the unit and create safety hazards.
General Questions,What if I need to extend my rental time on the day of the event?,Contact the rental company as soon as possible. Extensions are subject to availability and additional hourly fees.
General Questions,Can I use a water slide if it's not hot outside?,Water slides can be used as dry slides if the weather is cool—just don't connect the water. Confirm with your rental company that the unit is suitable for dry use.
Bouncy Kings Terms and Conditions,What areas do Bouncy Kings cover?,"Bouncy Kings cover Leicester, Derby, Coventry, Nottingham, Northampton, and Rugby."
