Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,Do I need to pay a deposit when booking?,The provided terms section does not mention any deposit amount or booking deposit requirement.
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,When does the hire start and end?,The hire starts on the date the goods are delivered and continues until the goods are collected by Ellis Leisure.
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,When do I have to pay the deposit and the balance?,"You must pay the deposit shown on the booking form when you sign the agreement, and you must pay the balance upon delivery of the goods."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,What should I do if the goods are not satisfactory when they are delivered?,"You should inspect the goods upon delivery, and if they are not satisfactory you must tell Ellis Leisure of any defect immediately."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,Do I need to insure the hired equipment?,Yes. You must keep the goods fully insured for their full replacement value against all risks prudently insured against for at least the whole hire period.
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,Can I connect other equipment to the hired goods or mortgage them to someone else?,"No. You must not mortgage the goods to anyone, and you must not connect any other equipment to the goods without prior written approval from ELLIS LEISURE."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,Will I be told my estimated delivery and collection times?,"Yes. You will be notified of the estimated arrival and collection times before your event, although the actual collection could end up being earlier than stated."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,"How much deposit do I need to send with my booking form, and who should the cheque be payable to?",A deposit of £20.00 per item hired must be enclosed with the completed booking form. All cheques should be payable to Ellis Leisure.
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,"Will I be charged if a payment I make by cheque, credit, or another method is not honored?","Yes. Ellis Leisure reserves the right to charge an administration fee of £50.00 for any payment made by cheque, credit, or any other form of payment that is not honored for whatever reason."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,What happens if I cancel my inflatable or related hire within 7 days of the event?,"If you cancel within 168 hours (7 days) of your event date, you will forfeit your deposit. Cancellations made at any other time incur no charge and any payments will be returned."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,"If I need to postpone or cancel because of Coronavirus/Covid-19 restrictions, what happens to my payment?","If your event cannot go ahead due to government restrictions, or because the venue has had to be closed because of a confirmed case, Ellis Leisure will accept transfer of the payment towards an alternative date, subject to availability, within 12 months of the original booking."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,How long can a deposit transfer be held for if I request a new date?,Transfers of deposits are limited to a time frame of 12 months unless Ellis Leisure specifically confirms otherwise.
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,"Who is responsible for loss, damage, or injury to a third party during the hire period?","The hirer indemnifies Ellis Leisure against any loss, damage, or injury to any third party arising through use of the equipment during the hire period, except where such loss, damage, or injury is caused by the negligence of Ellis Leisure, their contractors, sub-contractors, or their servants."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,"What happens if there is a delay, loss, damage or injury caused by something beyond your reasonable control?","We will not be liable for any delay, loss, damage or injury arising out of any cause whatsoever beyond our reasonable control."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,Which law governs the agreement and which courts have jurisdiction?,"The agreement is governed by and construed in accordance with the Laws of England, and the parties submit to the non-exclusive jurisdiction of the English Courts."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,What happens if I breach the agreement or become insolvent?,"If you breach any term and do not remedy a remediable breach within seven days of written notice, or if you become bankrupt, enter composition with creditors, have a receiver appointed, leave a judgment unsatisfied for more than seven days, or (if a company) enter liquidation or winding up, we may determine the agreement by written notice."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,Does the company give up any rights if it relaxes or delays enforcing the agreement?,No. Any relaxation or indulgence granted by the company will not be treated as a waiver of its rights under the agreement or as prejudicing those rights.
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,Can the inflatable be overcrowded or used by mixed-size users?,"No. The inflatable must not be overcrowded, and you must follow the user table on the unit. Do not mix the height or size of users."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,Are there any restrictions for users with health issues or during inflation/deflation?,"Yes. Do not allow anyone with a history of back or neck problems to use the equipment, and no-one should be on the inflatable during inflation or deflation."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,What happens if the balls are not all picked up and bagged before pickup?,"Unless all balls are picked up and bagged before their return, your £20.00 deposit will be cashed."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,What is the charge if footballs are lost or damaged?,"If any footballs are lost or damaged, you will incur a £20.00 charge."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,"Who is responsible for loss, malicious damage, or vandalism to the equipment while it is on hire?","The customer is responsible for any loss of equipment, and any malicious damage or vandalism caused, excluding normal wear, while it is on hire."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,What happens when I confirm a booking with Ellis Leisure?,"By agreeing to or proceeding to confirm a booking with Ellis Leisure, you are subject to these Terms & Conditions and also agree to Ellis Leisure’s terms and conditions of the hire contract."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,"Do I need to pay a deposit, and when does it need to be paid?","A deposit is required to secure the booking. The deposit amount is 20% of the total booking cost, and the balance must be paid before or on delivery."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,"Is a deposit required, and when is the final balance due?","A deposit is required to secure the booking, and the balance must be paid before or on delivery. The terms say the deposit is non-refundable if the hirer cancels."
Terms & Conditions of Hire | Bouncy,What happens if I cancel my booking?,"If you cancel more than 24 hours before the event, you are liable for 50% of the hire charge. If you cancel less than 24 hours before the event, you are liable for 100% of the hire charge."
Terms & Conditions,Do I need to read and agree to the Terms and Conditions before booking?,Yes. Bookings are accepted on the basis that the Terms and Conditions of Hire have been read and agreed.
Terms & Conditions,Will anyone be sent to collect the equipment on your behalf?,"No. The company states that, due to potential theft, they do not send anyone to collect the equipment on their behalf."
Terms & Conditions,What happens if the equipment is collected by someone other than Nicebounce Bouncy Castles?,You will be fully liable for new replacements and costs if the equipment is collected by anyone else except Nicebounce Bouncy Castles.
Terms & Conditions,Who is allowed to use the children's inflatable equipment?,"No adults should use equipment supplied solely for children's use. These units are intended for people below the age of 16 years, so no one over 16 should use the equipment."
Terms & Conditions,Does an adult need to supervise the equipment during hire?,Yes. A responsible adult over 18 years of age must supervise the equipment and children at all times. The supervisor must not be under the influence of drink or drugs.
Terms & Conditions,"Can I glue, stick, attach, or hang notices or signs on the bouncy castle?","No. Do not glue, stick, attach, or hang any notices or signs to the bouncy castle and equipment, as this can cause injury and may leave a sticky residue. Cleaning charges apply."
Terms & Conditions,Who is responsible for supervising children or vulnerable adults during setup and packing away of the inflatable and equipment?,"It is the Hirer’s responsibility to arrange adequate supervision of the children or vulnerable adults during setting up and packing away of the inflatable and equipment, and they must not touch the equipment during that time."
Terms & Conditions,"What happens if the equipment is damaged through misuse, neglect, loss, or failure to follow the conditions?","The Hirer will be liable for the full repair or replacement costs, plus any court costs or any loss of business resulting from the loss or damage, as per the hire contract."
Terms & Conditions,"Who is responsible for access, clearances, and underground services when equipment is delivered and secured?","The Hirer must ensure the delivery team has adequate access and clearances, and must inform Nicebounce of any known underground services before the equipment is secured to the ground using ground stakes (anchors)."
Terms & Conditions,Is the company responsible if children or vulnerable adults get hurt while the equipment is being set up or packed away?,No. The company states that it cannot be held responsible for children or vulnerable adults getting hurt on the equipment during setting up and packing away.
Terms & Conditions,"Can you charge a refundable deposit for an overnight hire, and how much is it?","Yes. For an overnight hire, a refundable £100 cash deposit may be requested if the castle is considered at risk of theft or damage by being left overnight at your premises."
Terms & Conditions,How far in advance do I need to cancel because of bad weather forecast?,"If you would like to cancel due to a bad weather forecast, the decision must be made no later than 24 hours before the hire."
Terms & Conditions,When is a full hire charge due on arrival?,"A full hire charge will be due if the inflatable does not fit, the location is unsuitable, the power is unsuitable, the surface type is unsuitable (for example artificial grass), the access is unsuitable, there is animal mess such as dog poo, or you have double booked them and another company."
Terms & Conditions,"When will you cancel outside hires due to weather, and do I get a refund?","We only cancel outside hires if the wind speed is forecasted over 24mph or there is heavy rain all day. If this happens, you will receive a full refund."
Terms & Conditions,Who should I contact if I am unsure about anything?,Please contact us on 07921124205.
Terms & Conditions,When is my booking confirmed?,"The hire agreement takes effect once it is signed, or once email correspondence has passed between B4 Bouncy Castles and the hiree confirming the booking."
Terms & Conditions,"Do I need to pay a deposit, and how much is it?","B4 may require a 50% deposit to be paid to secure the booking, or held as security against loss or damage of the equipment."
Terms & Conditions,What should I do when the equipment is delivered if there is a fault or damage?,You should check the condition of the equipment at the time of delivery and record any fault on the hire agreement.
Terms & Conditions,What is the late cancellation fee if I cancel less than three weeks but more than two weeks before the hire date?,B4 may charge a Late Cancellation Fee of 50% of the hire fee if less than three weeks but more than two weeks’ notice is given.
Terms & Conditions,Is there an extra cleaning charge?,"Yes. B4 may charge an additional £25 if the equipment is found to be excessively dirty, marked with face paint, or where glitter or similar contamination is present."
Terms & Conditions,Will B4 guarantee delivery and collection at the agreed times?,"B4 will endeavour to meet the agreed Delivery and Collection Times, but it cannot be held responsible for late arrival due to circumstances beyond its control."
Terms & Conditions,What happens if access for delivery is not available within 15 minutes of the agreed delivery time?,"If access is not available within 15 minutes of the agreed Delivery Time, B4 reserve the right to cancel the booking and recover the full Hire Fee."
Terms & Conditions,Who is responsible for supervising people using the equipment?,"Unless B4 has agreed to supervise use of the Equipment, the Hiree is responsible for ensuring that users are supervised at all times by a responsible adult and that the Equipment is used in accordance with the Safety & Operating Instructions."
Terms & Conditions,"Can someone with a back, neck, or other medical condition use the equipment?","No. Under no circumstances should anyone be allowed to use the Equipment if they are suffering from a back, neck, or other medical condition that may put them or other users at risk of injury."
Terms & Conditions,Who is responsible for safety measures when the equipment is being used?,"Unless B4 has agreed to supervise the equipment, the Hiree is responsible for putting in place appropriate safety measures to ensure safe use."
Terms & Conditions,Who is responsible for the equipment after delivery and before collection?,"Unless B4 Bouncy Castles has agreed to supervise the equipment as part of the Hire Agreement, the Hiree is responsible for the safe keeping of the equipment from the point of delivery until collection and will be held liable for any damage caused."
Terms & Conditions,"If someone is injured, how quickly must they seek medical assistance?",Any injured party must seek professional medical assistance within 2 hours of the incident occurring.
Terms and Conditions,What happens if the castle cannot be set up or used safely because of rain or bad weather?,"The text provided does not include any weather, rain, or bad-weather cancellation rules."
Terms and Conditions,"What deposit is required, and when is it paid?",The text provided does not include any deposit amount or payment timing.
Terms and Conditions,What happens if I need to cancel my booking?,"If you cancel for any reason, you will lose your deposit. Once a booking has been accepted, any cancellation means the deposit is forfeited."
Terms and Conditions,When will my booking be delivered and collected?,The terms shown here do not state exact delivery or collection times. They only say the hire is subject to the conditions in the agreement.
Terms and Conditions,What company do these terms and conditions apply to?,These terms and conditions apply to all bookings given to and accepted by 1-2-3 Bounce Ltd.
Terms and Conditions,Who will deliver the hired equipment and when?,Trained and uniformed members of staff will deliver the hired equipment on the date and to the address specified in your booking confirmation.
Terms and Conditions,What must happen if the hired equipment is returned soiled or damaged?,"The hirer must pay any sums incurred to cover cleaning costs at £15, plus any costs of repair, replacement and/or loss of earnings caused by the equipment being unavailable to be rehired."
View T&C's | Kings Bouncy Castle Hire,"How much deposit do I need to pay to secure a booking, and what happens if I cancel after paying it?",A deposit of 20% is required to secure your booking. The deposit is non-refundable if you cancel the booking.
